      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Aether-X1 NPU will operate across three primary voltage rails: VDD\\_CORE at $0.85\\text{V} \\pm 0.01\\text{V}$ with a maximum current draw of $15\\text{A}$, VDD\\_MEM at $1.2\\text{V} \\pm 0.02\\text{V}$, and VDD\\_IO at $1.8\\text{V} \\pm 0.01\\text{V}$. Clock frequencies are specified at a nominal $2.4\\text{GHz}$ for the compute cluster, with an optional boost mode reaching $2.8\\text{GHz}$ under peak load conditions. Thermal efficiency targets mandate a maximum TDP of $45\\text{W}$ at $90\\%$ utilization, achieving a power efficiency rating of $88.5\\% \\pm 1.2\\%$ across the operational envelope.",
      "source": "target",
